                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Surprisingly this game does not involve smacking heads at all. Players start at a menu with blinding graphics, with the “Start” button and controls slapped underneath it. Advice: Turn off “Hard mode” for the sake of saving your eyes. Trust me. From here on out, the entire experience I had was the same as any other platformer game, but with no tutorial or plot, cheap graphics and SFX that is atrocious. The flashing colors that coats the entire screen when you pick up a flower is an eyesore. The distorted screen if you go Hard mode is even worse - it affects the info bar on the top-right, making it unreadable. That’s more game-breaking than it is adding difficulty for players.  \n\nThe music felt generic and cheap, just like the rest of the graphics. Most of it looked like clip art ripped off from the web. That’s how low of a quality it is, and the Menu sounds were deafening to my ears. \n\nI had to stop within 5 minutes because all the SFX visuals were making me nauseous. Idk if the developer intentionally wants to cause motion-sickness for the players, but I do not recommend SMACKHEAD to anyone – especially if you are epileptic. The gameplay is bad, and the graphics were ick.",
